    'EN6-03-B: A companion is controlled while its owner already has the regular attached phase. The new order redirects only that phase\'s existing movement; it does not create an independent creature turn or charge the owner another Bonus Action. If a real grapple has set available Speed to zero, there is no travel and no stored push for next round. If suppression covered the route-issue opportunity, removing it later does not invent a retrospective route or replenish movement.'
