add('willbreaker', '''KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/F, one target unable to cast spells or use magic items and WIS ending saves. NEW select one perceived creature with line of effect. It makes initial WIS; success establishes nothing. Failure imposes the following source-owned restriction, concentration up to sixty elapsed seconds, with WIS repeated at each regular target END including an affected current turn's upcoming END. Outside initiative use the explicit END-only cadence. This supplies a finite ongoing duration in place of Core's preserved Instantaneous placeholder. No Charmed, Frightened, Incapacitated, Unconscious or generic mental damage is applied.

NEW spell restriction: the recipient cannot begin a new actual spellcasting commitment through any class, innate casting, item or other genuine spell source, regardless of RP price or omitted components. A paid zero-RP cantrip is still a spell. A nonspell class ability does not become one merely because it costs RP, is magical, or resembles a spell; use the actual source classification. An ongoing minute-long cast cannot perform future required spellcasting work while restricted, and ends/fails only under its own genuine interruption/work rule with already-paid costs retained. An instantaneous cast or Reaction already legally committed before this restriction established resolves through its existing stack; the restriction is not a retroactive Counterspell. A fully cast readied spell's later release is not another casting commitment and may still occur if its real concentration, release trigger and other permissions survive. Quicken's two separately paid child casts are each new commitments, so a not-yet-committed child is prohibited even if its parent was already cast.

NEW magic-item use means deliberate functional use, not every benefit from being near a magical object. The creature cannot intentionally activate, invoke or expend a magic item's properties, drink/use a magical consumable, command an item through its item-use interface, or wield a genuinely magical weapon/tool as the implement of an attack or task. A magic sword therefore cannot be swung as a weapon while this restriction operates; the creature may use an independently legal mundane weapon or unarmed profile instead. Wearing previously equipped passive magical armor, retaining a passive numeric item bonus, or benefiting from an independently running item effect is not automatically suppressed. An already active magic weapon does not turn mundane, and no property is erased globally. The recipient may safely carry, put down, give physical custody of, or remove an item through ordinary permissions; those handling acts cannot be disguised activations. Equipping an item specifically to invoke a new magical function remains prohibited; merely removing dangerous gear is not blocked.

Apply real present magical-item classification from the item's own profile/actual enchantment. An unrelated spell buff on a person does not make every held object a magic item. A remote non-item companion command remains a separate class/creature interface unless its actual source requires prohibited item use. A device that genuinely is a magic item is not exempt because it has wheels or another operator. Static attributes, already running allied buffs, the target's concentration and independently acting companions continue under their own dependencies. This is user-action restriction, not an antimagic area, dispel, broken item, drained charge or loss of spell knowledge. A source requiring future actual prohibited casting/item use fails at that future requirement; an effect requiring only ordinary concentration does not.

Known prohibited choices cannot be committed and spend no new spell RP or item charges. If a purportedly ordinary action is genuinely attempted on an item whose magical status is hidden, its ordinary committed action/work is spent before the functional use fails; no prohibited charge is spent and no special item-identification readout is supplied. Mere repeated declaration with no actual commitment is not an identification oracle. This proposal restricts specific action types while leaving other real Actions, Bonus Actions, Reactions and movement available, so it does not claim the whole-Action hard-control allowance. Actual defenses expressly covering these restrictions still apply. Independent Willbreaker instances keep their own casters, concentration, saves and deadlines; their prohibition does not stack in magnitude. Successful source removal/save, expiry, target death or concentration loss ends that instance. Suppression temporarily lifts it without restoring spent costs, old concentration, item charges or time; a later resumption bars only future prohibited commitments.''', [
    'EN6-04-A: A failed-save Wizard is concentrating on a previously cast wall, wearing passive enchanted armor, and holding a magic sword. Willbreaker does not end the wall or the armor\'s passive protection. It prevents a new cantrip and intentional attack with that magic sword; an ordinary unarmed attack, movement or Dodge remains available. A successful WIS at the target\'s actual regular END ends only this Willbreaker instance.',
    'EN6-04-B: A real readied spell was completely cast and paid before Willbreaker established. Its separately legal release can still occur without a new casting commitment. In contrast, a second Quicken child that has not yet committed is barred and pays no child RP. A legal spell already on the interrupt stack is not retroactively countered. If an unknown magical tool is actually used for an apparently ordinary task, the committed ordinary work can fail without spending a hidden charge or naming the tool\'s unseen properties.'
], 'NEW initial WIS/concentration minute/END saves, precise future-casting boundary, active functional magic-item ban including weapon/tool use, passive-effect distinction and hidden-status attempt costs.')

add('mental-prison', '''KEEP both Enchantment and Illusion placements, Action, 60 feet, V/S/F, one target trapped in an illusory reality and 5d10 psychic when entering or leaving. NEW select one perceived creature with line of effect and make an initial INT save. Success establishes no prison and deals no damage. On failure, if a genuine mental/illusion defense does not prevent entry, establish one subjective prison around that target. The fixed real boundary is the target's current axis-aligned occupied-body bounding box expanded five feet in each direction; it is not a physical wall, object, dimensional pocket or plane. Record the actual shape/anchor before damage. The caster's concentration maintains it for at most sixty elapsed seconds, an explicitly NEW duration replacing the preserved Instantaneous placeholder.

NEW entering is actual first establishment of this illusory state, not later movement into its former footprint by anyone else. On that one entry, deal 5d10 psychic to the recipient as an ordinary defended packet, with no second damage save. Its psychic immunity can prevent damage without preventing the separately admitted illusion. Charmed-only/Frightened-only immunity is not automatically illusion immunity. A defense that truly prevents the mental illusion prevents entry and its entry-triggered damage. Actual target death from entry ends the application with no postmortem exit packet.

Within the prison the target perceives its real interior occupants and objects, but a convincing opaque enclosure replaces its visual/auditory perception of the exterior. The invented enclosure grants no real cover, collision, sound barrier or support to anyone. Genuine unaffected nonvisual senses retain their real scope. The target cannot willingly move, self-teleport or accept transport across the fixed boundary while that belief/control component remains operative. It can move legally inside, speak, take other permitted Actions/Bonus Actions/Reactions, maintain concentration, and interact with actual interior targets. No Charmed, Frightened, Restrained, Speed zero or Incapacitated is added. Perception-dependent attacks/spells need actual available perception; attacks through the nonexistent physical wall otherwise obey their real unseen-target/line rules. Because ordinary Actions remain available and only a voluntary boundary/perception restriction is imposed, this proposed profile spends no whole-Action denial allowance. It creates no permission for a broader hard prison if a future implementation chooses to remove all Actions.

NEW the target may spend its ordinary Action examining the contradictions and make an INT/Investigation task check against the original spell DC. Success/Critical Success recognizes and leaves this mental state immediately; failure uses that Action and permits a fresh attempt on a later actual Action while the prison remains. This is an express repeatable escape action, not a generic unchanged-evidence skill retry. An actual source that specifically defeats the illusion retains its own success/removal permission; knowing that illusions exist alone is not a free removal. No external advice can forge a successful roll, though real evidence can support a separately applicable ordinary assistance rule.

NEW leaving is the first actual termination of the admitted mental state, including a successful escape, crossing its fixed boundary through independently legal involuntary displacement/teleport, normal expiry, replacement, voluntary dismissal or loss of concentration. That first departure deals one 5d10 psychic packet, then ends this application; a new real position outside the footprint never snaps back. Mark the exit entitlement spent before resolving the packet. The event has at most one entry and one exit packet per cast/recipient, no repeat crossing damage and no recursive exit on death caused by the exit packet. A target can be harmed on an ordinary ending even without physically moving; this is an explicit consequential reading of the entering/leaving clause. Suppression or an actually eligible dispel/removal that disables this source before departure prevents the exit payload and consumes that entitlement without banking it. Target death/removal also ends without a corpse packet.

If only temporarily suppressed, its original clock/concentration remain. It can resume the same still-live subjective boundary only if the continuing target is still within it; the entry does not replay and the already consumed exit entitlement cannot return. A target leaving the footprint during suppression ends the prison permanently; returning later is not a new entry. NEW only one Mental Prison can be established on a target across casters. A new failed-save, otherwise admissible application first ends/replaces the old one through its real exit procedure; after those consequences, recheck the same target's continuing eligibility before establishing the new entry. A saved-against or blocked new attempt replaces nothing. This makes repeated paid casts real separate events without infinite boundary or suppression loops. Real body position, other effects, resources and material evidence remain unchanged by the invented scenery.''', [
    'EN6-05-A: A target fails INT and actually enters the prison. The entry roll is 28 psychic before defenses. On its turn it spends its ordinary Action on Investigation, succeeds against DC16, and leaves the mental state; the independently rolled exit is 24 psychic before defenses. That cast produced at most52 raw psychic across its two actual events, not an additional 10d10 burst or recurring boundary tick. The escape Action was available because the prison did not impose Incapacitated.',
    'EN6-05-B: After entry, an eligible suppression field disables this prison. The departure entitlement is consumed with no suppressed exit damage. If the target remains inside and suppression ends before the original deadline, the same state may resume without new entry damage; its eventual exit has no refunded packet. If it instead moves outside while suppressed, the prison ends and crossing back into the old footprint does nothing. An ordinary unsuppressed concentration ending would have used the one live exit packet.'
], 'NEW INT entry save, fixed subjective geometry, concentration minute, movement/perception-only restriction and repeatable escape Action; precisely two maximum damage entitlements with explicit normal-ending, dispel/suppression and replacement rules.')

add('mass-suggestion', '''KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/F, up to twelve creatures, both school placements and the explicit Enchantment 24-hour course of conduct. NEW harmonize this one catalog identity to the Enchantment placement's concrete 24-hour duration for any genuinely acquired school version; retain the Illusion Instantaneous metadata as the conflicting historical source, not a second instant/permanent compulsion or an added casting grant. The current four class access rows remain Enchantment. No concentration is required. Declare one to twelve distinct perceived creatures within range and caster line of effect, and speak one reasonable finite course of conduct of at most forty ordinary spoken words. The same course is offered to all selected recipients, with only ordinary grammatical differences such as each creature's own carried item; it is not twelve unrelated orders hidden inside one sentence.

Each recipient must actually hear and understand the instruction through a language or genuinely applicable communication source. Hidden comprehension, reasonableness, feasibility and prohibited content are resolved after legal payment, not exposed as an identification test. Each eligible creature makes initial WIS. Success or an invalid instruction gives no new compulsion. Failure establishes the actual reasonable finite task for that recipient, lasting until its meaningful completion or at most 86400 elapsed seconds from resolution. One identifiable conditional trigger may be awaited inside that same original deadline; no later remote amendment or deadline extension is supplied. A recipient's failure/immunity does not free a new target slot after outcomes.

Use the reviewed Suggestion envelope in full: the creature genuinely pursues the task through its existing ordinary movement, ordinary Action and interactions. Its controller chooses reasonable effective methods and unspecified details. A reasonable ordinary hostile act can be compelled only when actually reasonable given that creature's real beliefs, loyalties, knowledge and circumstances; those facts are not disclosed to the caster. Ordinary Attack uses the actual native attack sequence and mundane ammunition, but not spells/RP, optional finite riders, magic consumables, charges, recharge/per-rest features or special expendable ammunition. Direct self-harm, knowingly serious hazard, unreasonable betrayal/murder of a recognized ally, protected private secrets, permanent surrender of materially valuable property and knowing binding-oath/duty violation remain prohibited. Bonus Actions, Reactions and separately granted extra Actions are not commandeered.

If the stated task necessarily demands whole ordinary Actions, including after a future trigger, reserve/claim its hard-control component once at successful establishment using the shared caster/recipient/encounter allowance. If that part is blocked, only an independently meaningful legal soft task actually contained in the original instruction may establish. A wholly blocked task creates nothing; no invented alternative objective or later deferred hard claim is allowed. A soft task never gains a whole-Action permission because a door later locks. Use a feasible alternative inside its original soft scope or end the remaining compulsion if none exists. Persistent instructions retain their establishment timestamp under Compelled Budget Arbitration; twelve recipients have separate actual budgets and defenses, not one pooled Action or shared mind.

No repeat save or separate damage-ending condition is added. Actual new violence or information may make the remaining task materially unreasonable, prohibited or no longer reasonably achievable; that recipient's compulsion then ends. Mere ordinary delay, brief incapacity or an obstacle with a reasonable permitted alternative does not automatically cancel a still-achievable finite task. Real food, water, care, sleep and work/rest limits remain; the spell cannot create a third work Watch, automatic crafting success, another assistant slot, an institutional office or fictional completed labor. A 24-hour order is not 24 hours of uninterrupted permitted work. Genuinely required expenses or materials must already be legal under the actual task/source rules; no forced optional resource debit is invented.

NEW one active Mass Suggestion task per recipient across casters. A later genuinely established Mass Suggestion replaces that task without refunding spent hard history; a saved-against or wholly invalid new cast does not. Different named compulsions, including reviewed Suggestion, coexist only through real budget arbitration and their own limits; this proposal does not silently erase their records. Suppression pauses execution, not elapsed time; no missed work, save, Action or route is queued. Recipient death, actual removal, completion or original expiry ends the task. Caster death alone does not end this nonconcentration instruction or provide a new deadline. After ending, no magical obligation, ownership, standing or consent survives, though actual completed mundane consequences remain.''', [
    'EN6-06-A: Twelve eligible guards hear one comprehensible reasonable instruction to deliver an ordinary message to a nearby safe post. Nine fail WIS and three succeed. Each failed-save recipient receives only its individually lawful task and its own original24-hour deadline; the three successful recipients are not replaced. If actual whole ordinary Actions are needed, each recipient\'s distinct hard-control history is checked at establishment. Nine controlled people do not provide nine extra Actions to the caster.',
    'EN6-06-B: A task begins at noon and has one permitted awaited signal. The signal arrives at8pm, leaving sixteen elapsed hours before the original noon deadline, not a new24hours. The target still needs its actual rest and ordinary work time; the instruction cannot manufacture an extra Watch or bypass the actual assistant cap. A target whose remaining task becomes an unreasonable betrayal after new facts ends that compulsion, while another whose task remains reasonable keeps its own deadline. The Illusion placeholder is preserved and its proposed duration harmonization awaits joint review.'
], 'NEW explicit24-hour harmonization of conflicting school metadata, WIS/comprehension, forty-word shared finite instruction, full reviewed reasonable-task and hard-budget rules, separate recipient endings and no extra work/rest rights.')

add('irresistible-dance', '''KEEP Action, 60 feet, V/S/F, a target using all Actions to dance and WIS ending saves. NEW select one perceived creature with line of effect and make an initial WIS save. Success establishes nothing; the title does not remove that initial resistance. On failure, attempt one whole-Action denial component under the shared source-character/target/encounter allowance and actual relevant defenses. If prevented or that allowance is already spent, establish no Dance and no invented soft fallback. Claim the allowance only on actual establishment. NEW concentration up to sixty elapsed seconds replaces Core's preserved Instantaneous metadata. The target repeats WIS at each actual regular END, including a current turn's upcoming END; outside initiative use the shared END-only cadence. An ending save requires no Action and can occur despite the dance.

NEW all Actions means every otherwise available full Action opportunity on any actual turn while this application is operative, including a genuinely granted extra full Action. The compulsory behavior is dancing as that full Action, resolved before a contradictory voluntary full-Action choice under the existing mandatory-budget procedure. Its priority is the Dance application's establishment time, retained through its duration. It grants no extra Action, performance success, movement allowance, attack, Dodge, casting or other Action task. A full Action spent dancing cannot simultaneously be an incompatible ordinary Attack/skill/casting Action merely because the player describes an attack as rhythmic. A narrowly defined extra attack that is not a full Action remains subject to its own actual triggering permission; this spell does not relabel it as an Action or grant its missing trigger.

Bonus Actions, Reactions, ordinary movement, speech and concentration are distinct and remain available under their normal rules. An extra turn does not supply a new ending save, but any real full Actions during it are still subject to the existing Dance. The spell cannot force a character to spend an optional resource that would grant an extra Action; if the character voluntarily obtains a new full Action while the restriction operates, that Action must satisfy the same actual mandatory instruction arbitration. An Action already legally committed before Dance established is not retroactively canceled, and already-resolved effects are never undone. Newly available uncommitted full Actions after establishment are covered. An earlier incompatible genuine compulsion can win its own shared budget through the existing priority rule; that does not dispel Dance or refund its hard-control claim.

Dancing uses whatever harmless motor motion the creature's actual body permits. Missing legs, Prone, a grapple or Speed zero does not grant automatic immunity or a fresh save; it attempts the dance with available motion and still spends the affected full Action. If all bodily motion is externally prevented but the creature otherwise has an available full Action, the compelled attempt still occupies that Action without moving its body, breaking an anchor or applying paralysis. Actual Unconscious/Incapacitated states retain their own stronger absence of permissions; this source never supplies a new Action to a creature that has none. No Speed reduction, attack advantage, saving-throw disadvantage, extra loss of concentration or forced self-harm is added solely from the dance. A source requiring future voluntary full-Action upkeep may fail through its own missed-upkeep rule; ordinary concentration alone is not such an Action.

For a companion on an original-owner attached chassis, NEW apply the compulsion only to an Action its real ordinary attached phase actually supplies, substituting the dance for that action without creating a new phase, commanding the owner to pay a Bonus Action or granting another offensive activation. Already-paid owner costs and structural reservations are not refunded when a pending attack becomes the incompatible action. Its repeat WIS save occurs at that actual original-owner regular attached phase's END, with no new creature START/END or resource refresh; a missing phase supplies no fabricated save or Action, while the original sixty-second maximum continues. Multiple Dance applications retain their own concentration, save and deadline records. A single genuine dance Action can satisfy their compatible demands without multiple charges to one Action budget. Suppression releases the demand while its clock/saves and consumed Action history persist; resumption affects only still-available future opportunities. Actual removal, expiry, target death or concentration loss ends that source, never returning the already spent hard-control allowance.''', [
    'EN6-07-A: The target fails its initial WIS and the caster has an available hard-control claim. Dance establishes. On a later actual turn the target has its ordinary full Action and one already-genuinely-granted Haste full Action: both available full Actions must dance unless a real earlier incompatible mandate wins the shared budget. Its Bonus Action, Reaction and actual movement remain separate. It succeeds on the free regular-END WIS save; the caster\'s hard-control history remains spent.',
    'EN6-07-B: A grappled target with Speed0 still spends an otherwise available full Action attempting the dance; it neither escapes the grapple nor becomes Paralyzed. An owner-attached companion gets no independent turn: its existing phase Action may be consumed by Dance and its actual phase-END provides the explicitly proposed save. Suppression does not restore an Action already danced away or refund an owner\'s paid command. A new Dance from a caster whose shared hard allowance was already spent establishes nothing.'
], 'NEW initial WIS, concentration minute/END recovery, whole-Action guard, every genuine full Action including extras but not BA/Reaction, mandatory-budget priority and anatomy/companion-phase completion.')

